[wille@hpcuhb.HP.COM writes:]
>Nethack 3.0 PL5 has been panicing on one of the players that I'm supporting.
>As part of the game's dying breath it tells the player to see me to try to
>rebuild the game for him and it leaves a '#####player.e.Z' file in the save
... {stuff deleted}
>1.  Exactly what is one to do with the '*.e' files that are created...
.
i believe Ken Arromdee recently posted a stopgap patch for the
Patchlevel 5 distribution which may cover this problem. the symptoms
sound right. panic save files (*.e) can usually be restored by renaming
the file by removing the ".e" suffix. you cannot force them (easily) into
debug (-D) mode. i'd suggest giving up on your version of the game
until you apply the stopgap patch.

